<title>INDIA: Indian aluminium, nickel rise on world prices.</title>
<headline>Indian aluminium, nickel rise on world prices.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aluminium and nickel prices firmed on Tuesday on higher world prices but other base metals were steady in listless trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>Aluminium rose 25 rupees to 7,600 rupees per quintal after gaining 125 rupees last week. Nickel gained 100 rupees to 36,900 rupees.</p>
<p>Copper was steady at 13,600 rupees per quintal, zinc at 7,950 rupees and lead at 4,150 rupees.</p>
<p>--Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
